    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim the cell-level type-swap accelerator or the partial-engulfment bias field are part of the Graner & Glazier (1992) Hamiltonian.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not model active chemotaxis, subcellular cadherin trafficking kinetics, or the fluctuation-dependence of sorting studied by Mombach et al. (1995).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D extended Cellular Potts Model (60^2, 68 cells) across all 5 thermodynamic regimes plus a 7-point continuous J_AB sweep, with a cell-level type-swap accelerator and, in the partial-engulfment regime only, an ad hoc symmetry-breaking field.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation of a confocal fluorescence embryoid body spheroid (`cell_sorting_specimen.jpg`) comparing empirical GFP/RFP radial occupancy against the 2D Potts core-shell profile (r = 0.925) and the 3D equatorial-section profile (r = 0.758).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: 3D extended Cellular Potts spheroid on a 64^3 lattice (840 cells, 26-neighbour adhesion, volume constraint, 8-colour sublattice-parallel Metropolis) with its 2D equatorial z-section, a Kawasaki-swap ablation and a 3D equal-adhesion control; logarithmic vs power-law fits of L_AB(t)/L(t) with exponents compared to the LSW alpha = 1/3 bound.",
        "reported_in_source: Foty, Pfleger, Forgacs & Steinberg (1996) Development Table 1: empirical Gallus gallus tissue surface tensions (20.1 > 12.6 > 8.5 > 4.6 > 1.6 dyn/cm) strictly predict transitive mutual envelopment.",
        "reported_in_source: Graner & Glazier (1992) PRL Eqs. 1-3: extended Cellular Potts Hamiltonian with interfacial tensions gamma_AB = J_AB - (J_AA + J_BB)/2 and gamma_tauM = J_tauM - J_tautau/2 partitioning parameter space into checkerboard (gamma_AB < 0), complete engulfment (0 < gamma_AB < gamma_BM - gamma_AM), partial engulfment (gamma_AB > gamma_BM - gamma_AM > 0), and dissociation (gamma_AM < 0); Fig. 3 reports logarithmically slow decay of the heterotypic boundary length.",
        "reported_in_source: Steinberg (1963, 1970) Differential Adhesion Hypothesis (DAH): dissociated binary embryonic tissues spontaneously sort into concentric core-shell or lens configurations governed by interfacial free energy minimization.",
        "transfer_boundary: 64^3 x 200 MCS is far from the asymptotic coarsening regime; exponents are fitted over ~2.3 decades of MCS including the initial transient, and the power-law vs logarithmic R^2 (0.9965 vs 0.9845 in 3D; 0.737 vs 0.769 in 2D) do not discriminate the two laws.",
        "transfer_boundary: The LSW alpha = 1/3 reference is a conserved-order-parameter coarsening bound, not an exponent measured for the Cellular Potts model; the Nakajima & Ishihara (2011) exponent is deliberately left null in the reference JSON because the paper could not be consulted offline.",
        "transfer_boundary: The vendored specimen is a Wikimedia Commons embryoid body, not a chick-tissue aggregate from Steinberg or Foty; the radial-profile comparison is a morphological analogy, not a reproduction of a paper figure." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Apical epithelial cell vertex polygon in Gallus gallus" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "5. Vertex / Potts / Nematics" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
