<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Steinberg (1963, 1970) & Graner-Glazier (1992) differential adhesion cell sorting — Code-to-model traceability: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-73) maps the Pass 3 additions function-by-function to the Lean theorems, the Chen et al. (2007) parallel-update scheme and the LSW bound, and names its own honest limits (L34-37); `simulate_potts_regime_3d` (L661-686) documents the Hamiltonian, update scheme, parity lemma, volume approximation and temperature rescaling; the volume-increment lines cite the Lean theorem (L800-801) and self-test check 9 numerically mirrors theorems 5-6 (L1600-1606). The math KG YAML registers the 3 new theorems. Deductions: the bias field (L390-394) is commented as a \"weak symmetry-breaking axis\" but neither cited nor flagged as outside the Hamiltonian, and the swap temperature factor 2.5 (L396, L770) is uncited (-4); the self-test docstring says 13 checks but the numbered blocks run 1-7 then 9-13 (L1595-1632) (-1); the 2D MCS convention (L409) and the T = 30 / lambda_V = 2 rescaling (L681-683) are asserted, not derived (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py L390–L396: Bias field commented only as 'weak symmetry-breaking axis'; strength 1.8 and acceptance temperature 2.5 T uncited <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py#L390-L396>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Steinberg (1963, 1970) & Graner-Glazier (1992) differential adhesion cell sorting — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Interfacial tensions and the 5-regime classifier (`compute_interfacial_tensions`, L137-181) match Graner & Glazier (1992) Eqs. 2-3 exactly and are mirrored by Lean theorems 1-2; the 2D Metropolis copy attempts (L399-457) and the new 3D solver (L646-854) implement Eq. 1 with the correct adhesion and quadratic area/volume terms, the single-voxel volume increment is proved (`potts_volume_energy_single_voxel_increment`), and the 3D sublattice-parallel update is exact for the adhesion term (theorem 5) with the volume-term approximation disclosed (L676). The 3D run reproduces complete engulfment (Delta_r = +0.198, control +0.004) and the Pass 3 item is genuinely closed (+2 vs v2 for the 3D Hamiltonian). Deductions: the partial-engulfment regime adds an external position-dependent field `dE += 1.8 * (x1 ... x2)` (L390-394) that is not in the Hamiltonian, so Panel A3's doublet lens is imposed rather than selected (-3); the \"Kawasaki\" moves at L361-397 and L747-771 exchange the types of two randomly drawn, generally non-adjacent cells at an uncited temperature 2.5 T — a non-local accelerator with no counterpart in the 1992/1993 papers, and the 2D kinetics are reported without the ablation that the 3D run has (-2); the 3D volume constraint is too weak against the 26-neighbour adhesion scale, leaving <v>/V_0 = 0.771 (L652-654, measurement `potts_3d_mean_cell_volume_fraction`), i.e. the cells are not at the target volume the Hamiltonian prescribes (-2); the 2D MCS is 1.5 attempts per boundary site (L409) rather than one attempt per lattice site, an uncited convention (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py L361–L397: 2D 'Kawasaki' type-swap accelerator between random (non-adjacent) cell pairs at temperature 2.5 T; no 2D ablation reported <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py#L361-L397>",
        "1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py L390–L394: Ad hoc symmetry-breaking field added to dE only in the partial-engulfment regime; not part of the Graner-Glazier Hamiltonian, imposes the Panel A3 lens <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py#L390-L394>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Steinberg (1963, 1970) & Graner-Glazier (1992) differential adhesion cell sorting — Morphometric validation: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1426-1546) now returns 15 measurements with references and units: the 8 Pass 2 metrics (tensions, Delta_r 0.367 vs specimen 0.279, L_AB/L 0.181, checkerboard 0.724, control |Delta_r| 0.017, profile r 0.925, Foty 10/10) plus 7 Pass 3 kinetics/3D metrics (alpha_3D 0.215, alpha_2D 0.189, alpha_section 0.207, swap-ablation delta -0.013, Delta_r_3D 0.198, section-vs-specimen r 0.758, <v>/V_0 0.771). `fit_sorting_kinetics` (L486-525) fits both the Graner & Glazier logarithmic law and a power law and reports R^2 for each; the 3D control gives alpha = 0.001 as a true null. Deductions: the reference exponent 1/3 is the LSW diffusive bound for a different universality class, not a value measured for the CPM, and the Nakajima & Ishihara exponent is null in the JSON (L246), so alpha is compared against a theoretical bound rather than a literature measurement (-4); fits span the whole 0..200 MCS record including the initial transient and the two laws are not discriminated (3D R^2 0.9965 vs 0.9845; 2D 0.737 vs 0.769, log preferred), with no late-time window or multi-seed uncertainty (-3); the 2D L_AB/L reference 0.14 (L1465) and the checkerboard reference 0.72 (L1472) have no stated provenance (-2); boundary length in 3D is counted on 6 face bonds (L600) while the energy uses 26 neighbours — consistent with the 2D convention but uncited (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/differential_adhesion_sorting/differential_adhesion_sorting_reference.json L236–L264: sorting_kinetics_2d_vs_3d block: LSW 1/3 and log limit as reference exponents; Nakajima & Ishihara exponent explicitly null (not consulted offline) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/datasets/differential_adhesion_sorting/differential_adhesion_sorting_reference.json#L236-L264>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-checkerboard-mixing-heterotypic-boundary-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-complete-engulfment-heterotypic-boundary-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-complete-engulfment-radial-core-shell-separation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-equal-adhesion-control-radial-separation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-foty-1996-chick-embryo-hierarchy-concordance>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-graner-glazier-gamma-ab-sorting>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-graner-glazier-spreading-tension-diff>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-potts-2d-power-law-sorting-exponent>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-potts-3d-equatorial-section-power-law-exponent>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-potts-3d-kawasaki-swap-ablation-exponent-delta>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-potts-3d-mean-cell-volume-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-potts-3d-power-law-sorting-exponent>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-potts-3d-radial-core-shell-separation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-potts-3d-section-vs-specimen-radial-profile-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-measurement-specimen-vs-potts-radial-profile-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
