<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Steinberg (1963, 1970) & Graner-Glazier (1992) differential adhesion cell sorting — MorphoEval overall 89.9/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py` after closing the single v2 remediation item: `simulate_potts_regime_3d()` (L646-854) runs the Graner & Glazier Hamiltonian on a 64^3 lattice holding 840 cubic cells with an 8-colour parity sublattice-parallel Metropolis sweep whose adhesion dH is exact by Lean theorem `parity_sublattice_sites_not_moore_adjacent`, and `compare_2d_vs_3d_sorting_kinetics()` (L857-904) tabulates power-law exponents for the native 2D model (alpha = 0.189, R^2 0.74, log law preferred), the full 3D boundary (alpha = 0.215, R^2 0.997, power law preferred), the 3D equatorial z-section (0.207), the swap ablation (0.228, delta = -0.013) and the 3D equal-adhesion control (0.001). The 3D spheroid sorts (Delta_r = +0.198 full, +0.224 section vs control +0.004) and both the 2D and 3D solvers are bitwise deterministic. The re-score is held near v2 (89.9 vs 90.5) rather than raised because the audit of the new solver exposed defects that v2 did not price: an ad hoc external field at L390-394 imposes the partial-engulfment lens of Panel A3; the \"Kawasaki\" accelerator (L361-397, L747-771) swaps the types of random non-adjacent cells at an uncited 2.5 T; the 3D volume constraint is not maintained (<v>/V_0 = 0.771 with lambda_V = 2, T = 30); the like-for-like 3D-section vs specimen correlation (r = 0.758) is weaker than the 2D one (0.925); and the three Pass 3 citations carry DOIs that could not be verified offline. Overall 89.9/100 (faithfulness 89.1, reproducibility 91.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 654cd6fc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 87, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/differential_adhesion_sorting_comparison.png: rendered output of 1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py at 654cd6fc, image/png, 740753 B, 3000×1890 px, artifact_sha256 6046cb66ae62af9e47d3b593c06f690c6b389ec313e42183a47ccced8c8cf39f (sha256 6046cb66ae62af9e47d3b593c06f690c6b389ec313e42183a47ccced8c8cf39f), spec_fingerprint 439c3a9015bc8fdc9014e2aa3a89cd71cffc876fcd81d0cb0b2f88bbf798d5a9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 439c3a9015bc8fdc9014e2aa3a89cd71cffc876fcd81d0cb0b2f88bbf798d5a9; artifact_sha256: 6046cb66ae62af9e47d3b593c06f690c6b389ec313e42183a47ccced8c8cf39f. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-differential-adhesion-sorting-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Steinberg (1963, 1970) Differential Adhesion Hypothesis (DAH): dissociated binary embryonic tissues spontaneously sort into concentric core-shell or lens configurations governed by interfacial free energy minimization. | Graner & Glazier (1992) PRL Eqs. 1-3: extended Cellular Potts Hamiltonian with interfacial tensions gamma_AB = J_AB - (J_AA + J_BB)/2 and gamma_tauM = J_tauM - J_tautau/2 partitioning parameter space into checkerboard (gamma_AB < 0), complete engulfment (0 < gamma_AB < gamma_BM - gamma_AM), partial engulfment (gamma_AB > gamma_BM - gamma_AM > 0), and dissociation (gamma_AM < 0); Fig. 3 reports logarithmically slow decay of the heterotypic boundary length. | Foty, Pfleger, Forgacs & Steinberg (1996) Development Table 1: empirical Gallus gallus tissue surface tensions (20.1 > 12.6 > 8.5 > 4.6 > 1.6 dyn/cm) strictly predict transitive mutual envelopment.; reconstructed_in_script: 2D extended Cellular Potts Model (60^2, 68 cells) across all 5 thermodynamic regimes plus a 7-point continuous J_AB sweep, with a cell-level type-swap accelerator and, in the partial-engulfment regime only, an ad hoc symmetry-breaking field. | Pass 3: 3D extended Cellular Potts spheroid on a 64^3 lattice (840 cells, 26-neighbour adhesion, volume constraint, 8-colour sublattice-parallel Metropolis) with its 2D equatorial z-section, a Kawasaki-swap ablation and a 3D equal-adhesion control; logarithmic vs power-law fits of L_AB(t)/L(t) with exponents compared to the LSW alpha = 1/3 bound. | Computer-vision segmentation of a confocal fluorescence embryoid body spheroid (`cell_sorting_specimen.jpg`) comparing empirical GFP/RFP radial occupancy against the 2D Potts core-shell profile (r = 0.925) and the 3D equatorial-section profile (r = 0.758).; transfer_boundary: 64^3 x 200 MCS is far from the asymptotic coarsening regime; exponents are fitted over ~2.3 decades of MCS including the initial transient, and the power-law vs logarithmic R^2 (0.9965 vs 0.9845 in 3D; 0.737 vs 0.769 in 2D) do not discriminate the two laws. | The LSW alpha = 1/3 reference is a conserved-order-parameter coarsening bound, not an exponent measured for the Cellular Potts model; the Nakajima & Ishihara (2011) exponent is deliberately left null in the reference JSON because the paper could not be consulted offline. | The vendored specimen is a Wikimedia Commons embryoid body, not a chick-tissue aggregate from Steinberg or Foty; the radial-profile comparison is a morphological analogy, not a reproduction of a paper figure.; does_not_claim: Does not model active chemotaxis, subcellular cadherin trafficking kinetics, or the fluctuation-dependence of sorting studied by Mombach et al. (1995). | Does not claim the cell-level type-swap accelerator or the partial-engulfment bias field are part of the Graner & Glazier (1992) Hamiltonian.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py:1462-1473 — the reference values 0.14 (2D L_AB/L) and 0.72 (checkerboard L_AB/L) have no traced provenance; either digitise them from Graner & Glazier (1992) Fig. 3 / Glazier & Graner (1993) and cite the figure, or relabel them as self-consistency targets.",
        "remediation needed: 1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py:1536-1538 and 1317-1332 — the like-for-like optical-section comparison (3D z-section vs specimen, r = 0.758, RMSE 0.256) is weaker than the native-2D one (r = 0.925) even though its Delta_r (+0.224) is closer to the specimen's (+0.279). Average the section profile over several z-planes near the equator (and/or over seeds) to reduce single-slice noise, and report which comparator the figure title treats as primary.",
        "remediation needed: 1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py:361-397 and 747-771 — the \"Kawasaki\" accelerator exchanges the types of two randomly drawn, generally non-adjacent cells (non-local type teleportation) at an uncited temperature 2.5 T. Restrict swaps to face-contacting cell pairs (C[c1, c2] > 0 in 3D; shared 8-neighbour boundary in 2D), cite or remove the 2.5 factor, and add the 2D ablation (`cell_swaps=False`) so alpha_2D = 0.189 and the log-decay r = -0.877 are reported with and without the accelerator as the 3D run already does.",
        "remediation needed: 1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py:390-394 — in the partial-engulfment regime the swap move adds an external field `dE += 1.8 * ((x1 if t2 == 1 else -x1) + (x2 if t1 == 1 else -x2))` that is not part of the Graner & Glazier (1992) Hamiltonian, so the doublet lens of Panel A3 is imposed rather than selected. Remove the field (or move the asymmetry into the initial condition), show that the lens still forms from gamma_AB > gamma_BM - gamma_AM alone, and add a self-test comparing centroid_offset with and without it.",
        "remediation needed: 1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py:486-525 and datasets/differential_adhesion_sorting/differential_adhesion_sorting_reference.json:244-247 — the exponent fits include the 0..~10 MCS transient and the two laws are not discriminated (3D R^2 0.9965 vs 0.9845; 2D 0.737 vs 0.769), while the only reference exponent is the LSW 1/3 bound and the Nakajima & Ishihara (2011) value is null. Fit over a late-time window (t >= 20 MCS), run >= 3 seeds for an alpha +/- s.d., and transcribe the published CPM exponent(s) once the paper is consulted.",
        "remediation needed: 1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py:64-72, datasets/differential_adhesion_sorting/paper_citations.bib:55-91 — the Mombach (1995), Nakajima & Ishihara (2011) and Chen et al. (2007) DOIs were entered from memory and are flagged unverified; verify them (CrossRef) and drop the \"not verified offline\" notes.",
        "remediation needed: 1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py:652-654 with measurement potts_3d_mean_cell_volume_fraction = 0.771 — lambda_V = 2 at T = 30 is too weak against the 26-neighbour adhesion scale, so 3D cells sit 23% below V_0 (min 31 voxels). Sweep lambda_V in {2, 5, 10} and T3d in {15, 30}, pick a pair with <v>/V_0 in [0.95, 1.05], and tighten the self-test bound at L1616 from (0.6, 1.1) to (0.9, 1.1)." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.99e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Steinberg (1963, 1970) & Graner-Glazier (1992) differential adhesion cell sorting — Parameter expressivity: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "All 5 regimes (Panels A1-A5), the 7-point J_AB sweep across both phase boundaries (`run_gamma_ab_sweep`, L528-560, Panel B2), the full 2D CLI (`--J-AA ... --seed`, L1646-1655) and, new in Pass 3, five 3D flags `--grid3d --mcs3d --T3d --lam3d --V0` (L1656-1660) wired through `run_all_regimes_and_render` (L1112-1117), plus the ablation (`cell_swaps=False`) and the 3D equal-adhesion control (L873-884). Deductions: no sweep exists in 3D (one J set, one T, one lambda_V), so the dependence of the 3D exponent on temperature or volume stiffness — the parameters that visibly misbehave (<v>/V_0 = 0.771) — is untested (-5); the 2D sweep runs 110 MCS at a single seed with no error bars (-2); the bias strength 1.8 (L394) and the swap temperature factor 2.5 (L396, L770) are hard-coded and not exposed (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Steinberg (1963, 1970) & Graner-Glazier (1992) differential adhesion cell sorting — Reproducibility package: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`--self-test` runs 13 checks in ~31 s (L1549-1641): SHA-256 and JSON structure, exact tension parity with Lean, sorting vs control vs checkerboard, log decay, specimen segmentation, Foty transitivity, two-run bitwise determinism for the 2D solver (L1596-1598) and for the 3D solver (L1628-1630), the parity lemma and volume-increment identity, 3D sorting vs 3D control with volume integrity, exponent windows and the 15-measurement contract. Default render ~29 s and the PNG is byte-identical across runs (telemetry step 6). Deductions: no requirements lock or pinned environment file for this slot (-3); the 3D volume self-test bound `0.6 < <v>/V_0 < 1.1` (L1616) is loose enough to pass a 23% volume deficit (-2); the GIF is regenerated but not checked for determinism (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py L1616–L1616: Loose volume bound 0.6 < <v>/V_0 < 1.1 passes the observed 0.771 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py#L1616-L1616>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-repro-package-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Steinberg (1963, 1970) & Graner-Glazier (1992) differential adhesion cell sorting — Source and data traceability: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`datasets/differential_adhesion_sorting/` carries the reference JSON (265 lines, 8 sources with DOIs), the SHA-256-pinned specimen verified fail-closed at runtime (`verify_reference_dataset`, L115-130; self-test check 1), `paper_citations.bib` (8 entries), `scout_manifest.json` and a README updated for Pass 3. Deductions: the three Pass 3 sources (Mombach 1995, Nakajima & Ishihara 2011, Chen 2007) have DOIs entered from memory and flagged `doi_verified_offline: false` in the JSON (L32-51), in the bib (L55-91) and in the module docstring (L72) — honest, but unverified (-5); the specimen's source page is a Wikimedia Commons upload with no species or staining metadata (README L25-27) (-2); the empirical reference values 0.14 / 0.72 used in two measurements are not traced to any table (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/differential_adhesion_sorting/paper_citations.bib L55–L91: Pass 3 BibTeX entries for Mombach 1995, Nakajima & Ishihara 2011, Chen 2007 with 'DOI not verified offline' notes <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/datasets/differential_adhesion_sorting/paper_citations.bib#L55-L91>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-source-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Steinberg (1963, 1970) & Graner-Glazier (1992) differential adhesion cell sorting — Morphological realism / specimen match: 87/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The SHA-256-verified confocal embryoid body specimen is segmented (L911-1010) into a GFP core (r_B/R = 0.49) and an RFP shell (r_A/R = 0.77, Delta_r = +0.28) and overlaid against the 2D Potts profile (Panel B4, r = 0.925, RMSE 0.210). Pass 3 adds the like-for-like comparator the specimen actually calls for — the equatorial z-section of the 3D spheroid (Panel C1, C4) — whose Delta_r_section = +0.224 is closer to the specimen's +0.279 than the 2D model's +0.367, and the 3D shells, section, 2D and specimen core profiles are drawn on one axis (L1317-1332). Deductions: the 3D-section profile correlation with the specimen (r = 0.758, RMSE 0.256, L1536-1538) is weaker than the 2D one, so the better-matched comparator in Delta_r is the worse-matched one in profile shape and the script does not reconcile the two (-4); the specimen is a Wikimedia Commons embryoid body of unspecified species, not a Steinberg/Foty chick aggregate, and panel crops, thresholds and the ROI radius are hard-coded pixel constants (L923-926, L936-937, L957) tuned to this one image (-5); the 3D section shows a visibly rougher core than the 2D panel (Panel C1) because cells are 23% under target volume (-2); the partial-engulfment lens of Panel A3 is produced with the bias field, so its visual match to Steinberg's lens is not a model outcome (-2). Credit for the explicit statement that the specimen is an optical section of a 3D spheroid (reference JSON L263)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py L1536–L1538: Measurement potts_3d_section_vs_specimen_radial_profile_pearson_r = 0.7584 against reference 0.95 — the like-for-like comparison is weaker than the 2D one <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py#L1536-L1538>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.7e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

