<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "(Pass 3) Sorting Kinetics — Logarithmic vs Power-Law Heterotypic Boundary Decay, 2D vs 3D" ;
    dct:description "Empirical kinetic comparison requested by the Pass 2 audit: exponent α measured on the native 2D model, the full 3D (64³) boundary, the 2D equatorial section of the 3D spheroid, a Kawasaki-swap ablation and a 3D equal-adhesion control (compare_2d_vs_3d_sorting_kinetics); no Lean statement because the fits are statistical, not algebraic | Variables: t: Monte Carlo Steps; α: power-law sorting exponent; R²_pow, R²_log: fit quality of the two descriptions on identical points" ;
    dct:source "Graner & Glazier (1992) PRL Fig. 3 (logarithmic 2D decay); Mombach, Glazier, Raphael & Zajac (1995) PRL 75(11):2244; Nakajima & Ishihara (2011) New J. Phys. 13:033035 (DOIs not verified offline); Lifshitz–Slyozov–Wagner coarsening theory" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py#L486-L525> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:notation "f(t) = L_AB/L_tot;  logarithmic: f = a + b ln(t+1);  power law: f = c (t+1)^(−α);  LSW diffusive bound α = 1/3 (R ~ t^{1/3} ⇒ L_AB/L ~ t^{−1/3}); logarithmic limit α → 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/jez.1401730406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cpc.2007.03.007>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1367-2630/13/3/033035>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.47.2128>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.69.2013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.75.2244>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.141.3579.401>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.122.5.1611> ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Differential Adhesion Cellular Potts Sorting (Steinberg DAH & Glazier-Graner-Hogeweg Hamiltonian)" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

